 "caveats": [
  "Joins are at serotype and year only. No establishment is linked to any outbreak, as the FSIS data licence requires.",
  "Outbreak-associated illness is a small, biased subset of salmonellosis; most cases are sporadic and absent from NORS.",
  "Public NORS currently ends at 2023 while FSIS sampling runs to FY2026, so the two series do not cover the same final years.",
  "Counts are small. Single large outbreaks dominate several serotypes, which is why pct_hosp_from_largest_row is reported alongside every total.",
  "NORS records can be revised after close-out, and recent years are under-reported because final data lag 12 to 18 months."
